# Archive/Legacy/scripts/ — Before-host quality gate scripts

User directive 2026-05-20 「下一步最该做的是把旧 Before quality gate 脚本退役或改名」
— retire the legacy Before-host quality gate scripts that no longer have a
target to test now that the Before iOS app was severed to `Archive/Legacy/`。

Per the substrate-wide discipline 「依旧 不删除 只 comment」 / 「不要 删除 创建个
文件夹 把 不需要的文件 都转移 进 文件夹」: scripts are RELOCATED here,not deleted。
Git history preserved through `git mv`。 Recoverable via `git mv` back to the
repo root if Before is ever revived。

## What lives here

| Item | Source path before | What it tested |
|---|---|---|
| `run_quality_gate.sh` | `/scripts/run_quality_gate.sh` | 20/20 release-floor gate against Before iOS app + BeforeUISmoke |
| `run_quality_gate_double.sh` | `/scripts/run_quality_gate_double.sh` | 40/40 double-difficulty gate (Before iOS + BeforeWatch) |
| `run_quality_gate_extreme.sh` | `/scripts/run_quality_gate_extreme.sh` | EXTREME gate (Before + non-determinism / drift / churn) |
| `run_quality_gate_x10.sh` | `/scripts/run_quality_gate_x10.sh` | X10 long-term-stability gate (Before iOS + BeforeUI + BeforeWatch) |

All 4 hard-coded `PROJECT="$ROOT/Before.xcodeproj"` + `xcodebuild -scheme Before`
/ `-scheme BeforeUISmoke` / `-scheme BeforeWatch`。 After Before severance these
paths resolve to `Archive/Legacy/Before.xcodeproj` (archived,not built),so the
scripts no longer execute against a live target。

Companion documentation moved alongside in `Archive/Legacy/docs/`:
- `QUALITY_GATE.md` (20/20 floor)
- `QUALITY_GATE_200.md` (200/200 apex aspiration)
- `QUALITY_GATE_DOUBLE.md` (40/40 pressure)
- `QUALITY_GATE_EXTREME.md` (extreme drift / determinism)
- `QUALITY_GATE_X10.md` (long-horizon stability)

## What replaced these gates (post-severance)

The substrate's own gates now run via SPM directly,no Xcode app shell required:

```bash
cd BehavioralAISubstrate
swift build         # clean SPM build, no Xcode required
swift test          # ~13k tests, ~85s sweep, 99.99% pass in isolation
```

CI gates in `.github/workflows/test.yml`:
- `bas-tests` — BehavioralAISubstrate XCTest
- `qinao-tests` — QinaoRuntimeSDK XCTest
- `boundary-checks` — 4 boundary scripts + schema parity + god-file guard

The `samplehost-tests` CI job is DISABLED until SampleHost gets a standalone
xcodeproj or Package.swift (was previously a scheme inside Before.xcodeproj)。

## Reviving any of these scripts

If a future host reintroduces an iOS app shell that needs xcodebuild-driven
quality gates,the easiest revival path:

```bash
git mv Archive/Legacy/scripts/run_quality_gate.sh scripts/
# edit ROOT,PROJECT,DESTINATION,scheme names to point at the new host
```

Or copy as a template — these scripts implement the 20-step counter + 5-axis
report shape that the substrate-side gates can re-use without the Before
xcodebuild coupling。

## Why archive instead of update

The substrate's current discipline post-MATURATION-ARC is SPM-first
(`swift build` + `swift test`),not xcodebuild-driven。 A meaningful
replacement for these scripts would require:
1. A target host with its own xcodeproj or Package.swift
2. A test surface that matches the substrate's L1-L14 layer coverage
3. UI smoke (currently SampleHost) running as a standalone build

None of these exist post-severance (SampleHost had no standalone build path
either),so updating the scripts in place would produce scripts that point
at nothing。 Archive preserves the templates for future revival without
maintaining broken-by-design files in the live `scripts/` directory。
